WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.200
Hi, I am Abhinav and I have built a platform like Lovable and Base44.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:09.700
You can type a prompt and it just turns it into an app.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:14.600
It's called App Foundry and I'll show you a real build.

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:22.600
Build a gym management app where the owner can track members, membership plans and pending

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.600
fees.

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:31.300
Show a dashboard with expiring memberships, overdue payments, today's check-ins and monthly revenue.

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:38.800
Add dummy data with members and one week of check-ins.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:47.300
So I've typed a prompt and I'll press enter and it starts building the app.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:54.200
So I've just sent the prompt in the backend App Foundry spins up a sandbox container with

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:56.100
a coding agent inside it.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:00.700
The agent writes the code, installs packages and runs the app.

00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:05.000
The important part is that the agent never touches the rest of the platform.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:09.500
It can only see its own code and commands it has written.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:17.000
So if it writes bad code or breaks something, it only breaks inside its own sandbox container.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:23.400
So that is what makes it safe for AI to write code and run commands.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:29.700
Every app also gets its own database separate from every other app with row-level security.

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:34.600
So when an app goes live, its data is walled off from everything else.

00:01:34.600 --> 00:01:36.600
So here the app is built.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:44.100
I can see the expiring members, the overdue payments, today's check-in and monthly revenue

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.100
of the gym.

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.900
You can also see the members here.

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:55.500
I can add members, the membership plan.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:03.000
I can also add the membership and plans and create plans.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:10.400
And who has paid and who has not paid the membership and the check-ins also.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:16.800
So it has built every feature that I talked about in the initial prompt.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:20.600
So just like that, any app can be built on this.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:26.200
And after the app is built, you can just hit publish and it publishes it with just one

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:26.600
click.

